   Technologies, FRANCE, DEC 05-08, 2023},
Abstract = {Federated learning as a distributed category yields sub-optimal
   performance for the presence of Non-iid in multi-domain data. To this
   end, we proposes a novel clustered federated framework for unsupervised
   multi-domain network anomaly detection, which implements dynamic
   clustered federated based on the data distribution of different domain
   so that each edge user learns the domain-optimized inference model.
   Compared to baseline, the proposed method enables users to obtain
   domain-optimal performance.},
